    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "While 演習 (enshū) semantically aligns with the target glosses 'practice, exercise, drill', especially in formal or structured contexts (e.g., military drills, academic exercises), it is not the most natural or common term for 'practice' in a general, daily_life context for a language learner. The English lemma 'practice' (noun) in its core sense often refers to the act of repeatedly doing something to improve skill (e.g., piano practice, sports practice). For this general meaning, 練習 (renshū) is the standard and more natural Japanese equivalent.",
